$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM EXPERIMENTAL. To 0.93 mL (0.010 mol) of 2-thiophenethiol was added 1.80
mL (0.013 mol) of 2-chloroquinoline in a 25-mL round-bottomed flask with
constant stirring and heating at 50 °C for 13 min. After cooling to 25°C,
the mixture was diluted with 20 mL ethyl acetate, extracted twice with an
equal amount of 5% sodium sulfite, and extracted once with an equal
portion of 10% sodium hydroxide. The organic layer was dried with
magnesium sulfate and decanted, and the ethyl acetate was allowed to air
evaporate. Then 2.20 g of solid 1 were obtained (91% yield). mp: 103-105
°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.97 (d, 2H), 7.72 (m, 2H), 7.63 (d, 1H),
7.45 (m, 2H), 7.20 (t, 1H), 7.01 (d, 1H). 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 119.1,
125.5, 126.1, 127.5, 127.6, 127.6, 129.0, 130.4, 133.5, 137.5, 137.6,
148.4, 164.3. IR (NaCl) 3428, 3000, 1100, 903. Anal. calc. 243.02 m/z
ASAP (+mode) 244.02 (C13H9NS2).
