$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of thioethers 8b-f Potassium
carbonate (85 mg, 0.61 mmol, 1.10 equiv.) was added to a solution of
thiol (1.13 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) and stirred for 15 min at room
temperature. A solution of
9-(2’,3’,5’-tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-2,6-dichloropurine 3 (250 mg,
0.56 mmol, 1 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) was added and the resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at 35°C (HPLC Control). Then the reaction mixture was
diluted with EtOAc (40 mL) and the organic phase was washed with brine (7
× 25 mL), dried over anh. Na2SO4 and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc; gradient 33%→66%)
provided product.
9-(2’,3’,5’-Tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-2-chloro-6-cyclohexylthio-9H-purine
(8f): A colourless oil. R f = 0.52 (hexane/EtOAc = 1:2). IR (KBr): 2934,
2855, 2104, 1755, 1748, 1563, 1434, 1371, 1336, 1235, 1048; 1H-NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 8.11 (s, 1H, H-C(8)), 6.19 (d, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 5.5
Hz, H-C(1’)), 5.79 (t, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, H-C(2’)), 5.58
(dd, 1H, 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, 3 J 3'-4' = 4.3 Hz, H-C(3’)), 4.44 (ddd, 1H,
3 J 3'-4' = 4.3 Hz, 3 J 4'-5a' = 3.9 Hz, 3 J 4'-5b' = 3.1 Hz, H-C(4’)),
4.41-4.37 (m, 2H,-H2C(5’)), 4.24-4.18 (m, 1H, H-C(cyclohexyl)), 2.15,
2.14, 2.08 (3s, 9H, H3COOC-C(2’,3’,5’)), 2.13-2.10 (m, 2H,-CH2-),
1.84-1.75, 1.64-1.47 (m, 8H, 4×(-CH2-)); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm): 170.3, 169.5, 169.3, 164.4, 154.0, 149.3, 140.8, 130.3, 85.9,
80.6, 73.1, 70.5, 62.9, 42.5, 32.7, 32.8, 25.6 (2C), 25.5, 20.8, 20.5,
20.4; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C22H28N4O7ClS [M+H]+, 527.1362; found
527.1362.
